# CORE RULES (pointer)

The block at the very top of `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` titled **CORE RULES (read first; these override everything below and any handoff or plan doc)** outranks this file, every skill, and every handoff or plan. Read it first.

- A finished unit is `npm run ship`. Never `git push` `main`, even if a handoff says to.
- No rebase, force-push, `git reset --hard`, or `--no-verify`.
- Nothing is sent unasked (emails, texts, CMAs, posts stay drafts).
- Never buyer or seller names in public copy. Never invent numbers or names.
- Prod DB is read-only unless Matt says otherwise. Never print secrets.
- Search the repo for existing API clients and keys before saying a service is not connected.
- When Cursor is out, use Matt's Grok subscription, never raw API keys.
- Unfinished work: push the branch, note `docs/plans/CROSS_AGENT_HANDOFF.md`, ask Matt short yes/no questions.

# Trunk + worktrees (anti-strand)

**Production truth is `origin/main`.** A finished unit is `npm run ship`. Never `git push` `main`. No rebase, force-push, or reset.

## Default

- Day-to-day work is a branch from current `origin/main`. A finished unit is `npm run ship`.
- Unfinished work is `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=8192 npm run push` plus a handoff line.
- Do **not** `git push` `main`. Do **not** use a long-lived release branch.
- No rebase, force-push, or reset.

## Worktrees are allowed when they help

Use a linked worktree for parallel agents, long experiments, or cloud-agent isolation. Not as a place to abandon unfinished work.

Required anti-strand rules (see **AGENTS.md → Worktrees**):

1. Name branches `wt/<agent-or-topic>-YYYYMMDD` (example: `wt/crm-mobile-20260726`).
2. Push the branch to GitHub right away. Do not keep the only copy local.
3. Before ending a session: push the branch. If work is unfinished, also record the branch, path, and intent in `docs/plans/CROSS_AGENT_HANDOFF.md` Current block.
4. A finished unit is `npm run ship` from that checkout. After it is on `main`: delete the branch locally and on `origin`, `git worktree remove <path>`, `git worktree prune`.
5. Never leave the only copy of valued work in an unpushed worktree with no handoff entry.

## Failure mode this rule prevents

Matt previously forbade worktrees because unfinished work got stranded off `main` and the other tool could not see it. Worktrees are fine. Invisible unfinished work is not. Push the branch right away.
